From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kkutysllb <46704313+kkutysllb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] chore(llm): upgrade pi-ai 0.82.1 -> 0.84.4 and adapt drift gates

The locked @earendil-works/pi-ai was two minor versions behind: its
model catalog missed recent releases (e.g. glm-5.3) and lagged the
provider-compat surface the upstream ships.

Adapter adaptations required by 0.84 (all enforced by the existing
drift gates):
- name new thinking format `baseten` and template var `thinking.budget`
- classify new compat fields (supportsFinishReason, chatTemplateArgs,
  thinkingTokenBudgetField, supportsThinkingTokenBudget,
  supportsAdditionalTools, allowedFallbackModels) as withheld
- map new stop reasons `pending`/`deferred` to error finishes
- 0.84 delivers caller aborts as error events carrying the raw abort
  reason, so toStreamChunks now takes the request signal and maps an
  aborted signal to the harness `aborted` finish
- dependency range widened to >=0.84.3 <1.0.0 so a plain
  `pnpm update @earendil-works/pi-ai --filter @deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-pi-ai`
  keeps tracking the latest 0.x catalog

Tests updated for catalog facts that changed upstream: deepseek gained
a `low` thinking level, DeepSeek endpoints now send `max_tokens`, and
installed catalogs are split by protocol (xai is responses-only, no
builtin provider mixes protocols anymore).

Verified: pnpm -w run build:lib:host clean; vitest packages/llm +
packages/bundle/base 940/940 green.
---
Archive note (KCoder upstream/ bookkeeping, 2026-09-01):
This archive now covers BOTH pi-ai upgrade commits on the fork
integration branches, renamed 0.84.3 -> 0.84.4 to match the final state:

- Segment 1 (below, unchanged): 0.82.1 -> 0.84.3 (dbb80cc08f,
  chore/pi-ai-0.84.3-upgrade) — all adapter/catalog/stream adaptations.
- Segment 2 (appended): 0.84.3 -> 0.84.4 (ed5871ff61,
  chore/pi-ai-0.84.4-upgrade) — dependency declaration narrowed to
  ^0.84.4 and a duplicated dsh-launch-environment row removed; the
  lockfile / patchedDependencies-key / THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES changes of
  that commit live in the fork repo, not in this source archive (the
  relay patches over the pi-ai package itself are archived as 0003/0004).

Reference-only: setup.sh consumes the kcoder/alpha.3 integration branch
directly. This file does NOT apply cleanly onto the upstream alpha.3
baseline tree (two merge conflicts were resolved manually on the
integration branch: llm-pi-ai/package.json x2); kept as a faithful
record of what the fork changes, in commit order.

